 stages",[79,80,81],"stages","Gameplay & code","Engines & scenes","Testing","Topics",[85,86,87,88,89],"tags","Windows","Accessibility","Native GUI","CUA","DPI","Further reading",[92,93,94,95,96],{"_51":105,"_25":106},{"_51":103,"_25":104},{"_51":101,"_25":102},{"_51":99,"_25":100},{"_51":97,"_25":98},"GameMap: native UI evidence boundaries","https://github.com/OpenEnvision/GameMap/blob/main/docs/engine-operation-contracts.md#native-gui-automation-is-a-separate-evidence-surface","Window/display capture and frame lifetime","https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/apps/develop/media-authoring-processing/screen-capture","DPI coordinates","https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/winauto/uiauto-screenscaling","Input and integrity limits","https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/winuser/nf-winuser-sendinput","Properties and occlusion","https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/winauto/uiauto-automation-element-propids","Project source",[109],{"_51":107,"_25":57},"Why it belongs here","Provider support must be probed per control; no specific game editor is assumed accessible. UIA coordinates are physical pixels, while absolute mouse input uses normalized desktop coordinates. Bounding rectangles may contain occluded points, foreground activation can be refused, and input insertion does not prove application completion. Integrity restrictions must be respected.","detail","guidance","Resource type","Documentation","Category","Game production","category","lead","summary","name","production","docs",[133,134,135,136,137],[85,86,87,88,89],[130,131,132],[128,129],"2d","3d","code","scene","test",{"_51":105,"_25":106},{"_51":103,"_25":104},{"_51":101,"_25":102},{"_51":99,"_25":100},{"_51":97,"_25":98},{"_139":140},"documents",{"_141":142,"_143":144},"en",[146,150,151,152,149,153,154,155,156,157,158,159,160,161,162,163,164,165,166,167,168,169,170,171,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,148,185,147,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196,